Here's a sample End User API for 3D Camera Animation in TypeScript:
```typescript
import { Camera, Scene } from 'three';

class AnimationAPI {
  private scene: Scene;
  private camera: Camera;

  constructor(scene: Scene, camera: Camera) {
    this.scene = scene;
    this.camera = camera;
  }

  public animate() {
    requestAnimationFrame(() => this.animate());
    this.update();
  }

  public update() {
    this.camera.position.x += 0.1;
    this.camera.position.y += 0.1;
    this.camera.position.z += 0.1;

    this.scene.render();
  }
}

const scene = new Scene();
const camera = new Camera();
camera.position.set(0, 0, 5);

const animationAPI = new AnimationAPI(scene, camera);
animationAPI.animate();
```
This API provides a simple way to animate a 3D camera in a Three.js scene. The `animate` method requests the next frame and updates the camera position, while the `update` method renders the scene with the updated camera position.

