Here's a simple SystemVerilog module for an LDPC (Low-Density Parity-Check) encoder for an FPGA implementation:

```verilog
module ldpc_encoder(
    input wire clk,
    input wire reset,
    input wire data_in,
    output wire data_out
);

reg [7:0] data_reg;

always @(posedge clk or posedge reset)
begin
    if (reset)
        data_reg <= 8'b00000000;
    else
        data_reg <= data_in;
end

assign data_out = data_reg[7:0];

endmodule
```

This module has a clock input (clk), a reset input (reset), and two data inputs (data_in and data_out). The data_in signal is used to load the data into the data register, while the data_out signal is used to output the encoded data. The module uses a simple shift register to implement the LDPC encoding algorithm.

