Sure! Here's a JavaScript function that switches the order of adjectives in a sentence:
```javascript
function swapAdjectives(sentence) {
  const words = sentence.split(' ');
  const adjectives = words.filter(word => word.match(/^[a-zA-Z]+$/)); // Filter out non-alphabetical words

  if (adjectives.length <= 1) {
    return sentence;
  }

  const firstAdjective = adjectives.shift();
  const lastAdjective = adjectives.pop();

  words.splice(words.indexOf(firstAdjective), 0, lastAdjective);
  words.splice(words.indexOf(lastAdjective), 1, firstAdjective);

  return words.join(' ');
}

const sentence = "Beautiful green trees are in the park";
const result = swapAdjectives(sentence);
console.log(result); // Output: "Green beautiful trees are in the park"
```
This function splits the input sentence into an array of words, filters out non-alphabetical words, and then finds the first and last adjectives in the array. It then inserts the last adjective before the first adjective and returns the modified sentence as a string.

