To use the `updateAAD` method in the AEAD GCM cipher class for authentication, follow these steps:

1. Import the necessary classes:
```java
import javax.crypto.Cipher;
import javax.crypto.spec.IvParameterSpec;
import javax.crypto.spec.SecretKeySpec;
import com.google.crypto.tink.aead.Aead;
import com.google.crypto.tink.aead.AeadParameters;
import com.google.crypto.tink.aead.AeadSivParameterSpec;
```
2. Create an instance of the AEAD cipher class:
```java
Aead aead = Aead.newInstance("AES/GCM/NoPadding");
```
3. Set the encryption key and initialization vector (IV):
```java
byte[] key = "your_encryption_key".getBytes();
byte[] iv = "your_initialization_vector".getBytes();

SecretKeySpec secretKeySpec = new SecretKeySpec(key, "AES");
IvParameterSpec ivParameterSpec = new IvParameterSpec(iv);
```
4. Initialize the AEAD cipher with the key and IV:
```java
aead.init(Cipher.ENCRYPT_MODE, secretKeySpec, ivParameterSpec);
```
5. Use the `updateAAD` method to authenticate data:
```java
byte[] data = "your_data_to_authenticate".getBytes();
byte[] tag = aead.updateAAD(data);
```
6. Verify the authenticity of the data using the `verifyAAD` method:
```java
boolean isAuthentic = aead.verifyAAD(data, tag);
```

Note that the `updateAAD` and `verifyAAD` methods are only available in the Google Cloud Tink library, which is a cryptographic library that provides secure and efficient primitives for encryption, decryption, and more. You can download the library from the official website: https://github.com/google/tink

