Here's the HTML code for creating a web page that displays an image with a caption underneath it, and makes the image a hyperlink to another web page:

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
  <head>
    <title>Image with Caption</title>
    <style>
      #img-container {
        text-align: center;
      }
      #img-container img {
        max-width: 100%;
        height: auto;
      }
      #img-container p {
        margin: 0;
        font-style: italic;
      }
    </style>
  </head>
  <body>
    <div id="img-container">
      <a href="http://www.example.com"><img src="image.jpg" alt="Image"></a>
      <p>Caption goes here</p>
    </div>
  </body>
</html>
```

This code creates a div element with an ID of "img-container", which contains an anchor tag (`<a>`) that links to another webpage (`http://www.example.com`). The `<img>` tag within the anchor tag specifies the source of the image (`image.jpg`) and its alternative text (`Image`). Below the image, there is a paragraph element (`<p>`) that contains the caption for the image. The `text-align: center;` style property centers the image and caption horizontally, while the `max-width: 100%;` and `height: auto;` properties ensure that the image resizes responsively to different screen sizes. Finally, the `font-style: italic;` style property adds some visual interest to the caption by making it italicized.

To utilize Java programming language for blending different audio files and creating a realistic experience of a summer day, you can use libraries such as SoX (Sound eXchange) or PortAudio. These libraries allow you to read, process, and write audio files in various formats.

Here's a simple example using SoX:

1. Add the SoX dependency to your project:
```xml
<dependency>
    <groupId>org.sox</groupId>
    <artifactId>sox</artifactId>
    <version>14.4.2</version>
</dependency>
```

2. Create a Java class to blend the audio files:
```java
import org.sox.Sox;
import org.sox.SoxException;

public class AudioBlender {
